From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: describe the TCSR download-mode cookie

Describe the TCSR register block and point qcom_scm at its download-mode
cookie, as SM8550 and SM8650 already do. Download mode stays off unless
it is requested with qcom_scm.download_mode or at runtime through
/sys/module/qcom_scm/parameters/download_mode. When enabled, a crash or
watchdog reset can enter the boot ROM's RAM dump mode instead of
rebooting, so the dump can be collected over USB.

On SM8750 the TCSR clock controller moved to its own block, so the TCSR
at 0x1fc0000 has no other user and is described as a plain syscon. The
base, size and 0x19000 offset match the vendor sun.dtsi.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
index 2983669..a24ca19 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -230,6 +230,7 @@
 			compatible = "qcom,scm-sm8750", "qcom,scm";
 			interconnects = <&aggre2_noc MASTER_CRYPTO QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
 					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
+			qcom,dload-mode = <&tcsr 0x19000>;
 		};
 
 		scmi {
@@ -2190,6 +2191,11 @@
 			#hwlock-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		tcsr: syscon@1fc0000 {
+			compatible = "syscon";
+			reg = <0x0 0x01fc0000 0x0 0x30000>;
+		};
+
 		remoteproc_mpss: remoteproc@4080000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,sm8750-mpss-pas";
 			reg = <0x0 0x04080000 0x0 0x10000>;
